' ============================================================================
' EdgeIteration_scripts.puml
'
' Purpose : PlantUML sequence diagrams for the @NikolaiGogol / _scripts
'           edge-iteration workflow on @terra, one scenario per diagram
'           (S0..S9) so each operator path stays readable.
' RFC     : docs/rfc/RFC-0001-edge-iteration-workflow.md
' Scenarios: docs/rfc/RFC-0001-edge-iteration-scenarios.md (authoritative
'           analyst catalogue; this file renders S0..S9 from it).
' Date    : 2026-10-29
' Base    : 004ee9e
'
' Shared facts:
'   source    = $HOME/.bookmarks/shared-projects/ChronoIndex/2026/ConvPlatProv-HomeServer__HomeAssistant/@NikolaiGogol
'   target    = /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts
'   container = HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol
'
' Phase 0 = deploy scripts as-is.
'   /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts is a DEBUG SURFACE:
'   no bind mount, no compose change, tags [scripts, debug], and it is not
'   implied by `container`. It is not the deployment path.
'
' Style: one start/end block per scenario, autonumber per diagram,
'        participants declared only where used (cf. docs/Deploy#NixContainer.puml).
' ============================================================================


' ============================================================================
' Header / legend block
' ============================================================================
@startuml
title EdgeIteration_scripts — Shared facts and diagram index
legend
source:    $HOME/.bookmarks/shared-projects/ChronoIndex/2026/ConvPlatProv-HomeServer__HomeAssistant/@NikolaiGogol
target:    /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts
container: HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol
Phase 0 = deploy scripts as-is; _scripts is a debug surface with no bind mount,
no compose change, tags [scripts, debug], and no implication from container.

S0 full deploy; S1 scripts-only; S2 remote edit; S3 in-container rebuild;
S4 promotion; S5 ref pinning; S6 VM lifecycle; S7 remote check; S8 drift;
S9 reverse flow (pull the on-@terra edits back).
endlegend
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S0 - Full authoritative deploy
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S0 — Full authoritative deploy (TAGS=image,container,scripts)

actor Operator
participant "Control node" as ControlNode
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "Docker daemon" as Docker
participant "Container\nHomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol" as Container
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir

Operator -> ControlNode : make --directory=[Unix_dotfiles] build-NikolaiGogol (artifact precondition)
Operator -> ControlNode : run TAGS=image,container,scripts
ControlNode -> Ansible : ansible-playbook -i hosts.ini deploy-nikolaigogol.yml --tags image,container,scripts
== Artifact identity on the control node ==
Ansible -> ControlNode : stat result-NikolaiGogol tarball and compute sha256
Ansible -> ControlNode : invoke conv-plat-prov.content-tag and assert it equals the sha256 slice
ControlNode --> Ansible : artifact path, sha256 and 12-hex content tag
== Image transfer and load ==
Ansible -> Terra : rsync --checksum tarball to /zterra/local-/var-/cache/nixos-images/[sha].tar.xz
Ansible -> Docker : docker image inspect ds-omega/nikolaigogol with tag [sha12]
alt image absent
    Ansible -> Docker : docker import [sha].tar.xz as ds-omega/nikolaigogol with tag [sha12]
else image already loaded
    Ansible -> Ansible : skip docker import
end
Docker --> Ansible : image present after inspect
opt TBD (planned) dependency layers (HAOS, Unix_dotfiles, Virt_scripts)
    Ansible -> Terra : rsync HAOS 16.3 qcow2 to shared-/@Manilov/dotfiles-/_configs/HomeAssistant__/
    Ansible -> Terra : rsync Unix_dotfiles and Virt_scripts at their pinned shas
    Terra -> Terra : verify payload digests and write dependency .deploy-state files
end
note over Ansible, Terra
  Dependency roles are planned in the dependency-layer plan and absent at base HEAD.
  When disabled, the three bind sources must already exist; HAOS fails closed.
end note
== Container recreate ==
Ansible -> Terra : render docker-compose-system.yml and .env from group vars
Ansible -> Terra : docker compose -f docker-compose-system.yml config -q
Ansible -> Docker : community.docker.docker_compose_v2 state=present pull=never
Docker -> Container : recreate only when the rendered config changed
Container --> Ansible : container running with image ds-omega/nikolaigogol tag [sha12]
== Phase 0 scripts surface ==
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync upstream @NikolaiGogol with delete=false and the Phase 0 excludes
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : render .env with mode 0600
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash the deployed tree and write .deploy-state when absent or changed
Ansible -> Terra : bash -n each deployed *.sh
Ansible -> Terra : docker compose -f docker-compose-system.yml config -q
Ansible -> Terra : make -n image-name
Terra --> Ansible : all three checks exit 0
Ansible --> Operator : report image, container and scripts result
note over ScriptsDir
  Debug surface only: no bind mount and no compose change.
  Tags [scripts, debug] are independent of `container`; TAGS=image,container
  leaves _scripts untouched. A scripts failure occurs after the container deploy.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S1 - Scripts-only deploy, Phase 0
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S1 — Scripts-only deploy (Phase 0)

actor Operator
participant "Control node" as ControlNode
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir

Operator -> ControlNode : run TAGS=scripts via Makefile.NixosScripts
ControlNode -> Ansible : ansible-playbook -i hosts.ini deploy-nikolaigogol.yml --tags scripts
Ansible -> ControlNode : assert source dir, switch-nixos.sh and Makefile exist
alt source assertion fails
    Ansible --> Operator : fail with the expected upstream path and remediation
else source complete
    Ansible -> Terra : ensure _scripts exists with mode 0755
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : read .deploy-state when present
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash target tree excluding .env and .deploy-state*
    ScriptsDir --> Ansible : current tree_sha256
    alt clean (no manifest or tree_sha256 matches)
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync --checksum --omit-dir-times with delete=false
        note right of Ansible
          Excludes: .git, .env, result-*,
          node_modules, .yarn/cache
        end note
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : render .env with mode 0600
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash deployed tree and write .deploy-state when absent or changed
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : bash -n each *.sh
        Ansible -> Terra : docker compose -f docker-compose-system.yml config -q
        Ansible -> Terra : make -n image-name
        Terra --> Ansible : verification exit 0
        Ansible --> Operator : report scripts path, changed state and verification
    else drift (hash differs and force=false)
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : sha256sum -c .deploy-state.drift
        Ansible --> Operator : fail and list the drifted paths
        Operator -> Ansible : re-run with -e nikolaigogol_scripts_force=true
        Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync overwrite, render .env, rewrite manifest
        Ansible --> Operator : report forced deploy
    end
end
note over ScriptsDir
  delete=false leaves stale files and debugger additions in place.
  The manifest and drift report are the visibility mechanism.
  Missing docker or make skips only that validation probe; the role continues.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S2 - Ad-hoc debug/edit on the remote host
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S2 — Ad-hoc debug/edit on @terra

actor Operator
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "Docker daemon" as Docker
participant "Container\nHomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol" as Container
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir

Operator -> Terra : ssh terra
Terra -> ScriptsDir : cd /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts
Operator -> ScriptsDir : edit a script, docker-compose-system.yml or .env
Operator -> ScriptsDir : bash -n [edited script].sh
alt compose file edited
    Operator -> Terra : docker compose -f docker-compose-system.yml config -q
    Terra -> Docker : validate compose with the rendered .env
    Docker --> Terra : exit 0
end
opt Makefile or target edited
    Operator -> ScriptsDir : make -n [changed target]
end
Operator -> Terra : make stop-system-container
Terra -> Docker : sudo docker stop HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol
Operator -> Terra : make rm-system-container
Terra -> Docker : sudo docker rm HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol
Operator -> Terra : make import-nixos
Terra -> Docker : sudo docker import tarball and tag the debug image
Operator -> Terra : make start-system
Terra -> Docker : sudo docker compose up --detach
Docker -> Container : recreate and start the managed container
Operator -> Terra : ./connect.sh or make connect-nixos
Terra -> Container : docker exec -it --user ds13 ... bash
note over Operator, Container
  This path bypasses roles/nikolaigogol_scripts and can race the
  Ansible-managed container. Two writers to the same container is
  undefined behaviour, and the recreate drops container-layer state.
  No Ansible report or .deploy-state update is produced; a later S1/S0
  re-renders .env and treats edited payload files as drift (S8).
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S3 - Edge config iteration inside the container
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S3 — Edge config iteration inside the container

actor Operator
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "Container\nHomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol" as Container

Operator -> Terra : ssh terra
Terra -> Container : docker exec -it --user ds13 HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol bash
Operator -> Container : edit /home/ds13/.bookmarks/shared-configs/Unix_dotfiles
alt test (default edge loop)
    Operator -> Container : nixos-rebuild test --flake /home/ds13/.bookmarks/shared-configs/Unix_dotfiles#NikolaiGogol
    Container -> Container : activate the new system for this boot
    Container --> Operator : no boot entry created
else switch (explicit edge-commit)
    Operator -> Container : nixos-rebuild switch --flake /home/ds13/.bookmarks/shared-configs/Unix_dotfiles#NikolaiGogol
    Container -> Container : write a container-local boot generation
    Container --> Operator : generation survives restart, not recreate
end
Operator -> Container : observe HomeAssistant and @Manilov behaviour
opt rollback
    Operator -> Container : nixos-rebuild --rollback switch
    Container --> Operator : previous generation restored
end
note over Container
  A source edit in the Unix_dotfiles bind may survive, but the activation,
  installed packages, /etc edits, units and rebuild generations are ephemeral.
  docker rm or recreate discards them; a switch is not promotion.
  Promotion is commit, then pin, then image deploy (S4).
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S4 - Promotion of an edge fix
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S4 — Promotion of an edge fix

actor Operator
participant "Upstream repos\nUnix_dotfiles / Virt_scripts" as UpstreamRepos
participant "Pins" as Pins
participant "Control node" as ControlNode
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "Docker daemon" as Docker
participant "Container\nHomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol" as Container
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir

Operator -> UpstreamRepos : commit the verified edge fix
UpstreamRepos --> Operator : commit sha
Operator -> Pins : refs-update REF=[commit sha]
Pins --> Operator : pin variable set to the 40-hex sha
Operator -> ControlNode : build the artifact from the pinned checkout
Operator -> Ansible : run the full authoritative deploy S0 (TAGS=image,container,scripts)
Ansible -> Terra : sync dependencies at the pin and load the content-tagged image
Terra -> Docker : docker import image as ds-omega/nikolaigogol with tag [sha12]
Docker -> Container : recreate HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol from the new image
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : refresh _scripts only when the scripts tag is included
Container --> Operator : edge fix promoted, container-layer state discarded
Operator -> Terra : verify with S7; for VM definitions also run S6
note over UpstreamRepos, Container
  There is no copy-out path from the edge loop.
  The source commit is the only promotion artifact.
  A script-only change may leave the image unchanged; a VM-definition-only
  change still needs the domain redefined in S6.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S5 - Dependency ref pinning
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S5 — Dependency ref pinning (refs-list and refs-update)

actor Operator
participant "Pins" as Pins
participant "Upstream repos\nVirt_scripts / Unix_dotfiles" as UpstreamRepos
participant "Control node" as ControlNode
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra

Operator -> Pins : make refs-list
Pins -> UpstreamRepos : resolve the configured ref
UpstreamRepos --> Pins : 40-hex sha and commit subject
Pins --> Operator : repo, configured ref, resolved sha, subject
Operator -> Pins : make refs-update [REF=[ref]]
alt REF supplied
    Pins -> UpstreamRepos : resolve REF
else no REF supplied
    Pins -> UpstreamRepos : resolve the configured default branch (main for Virt_scripts, dev for Unix_dotfiles)
end
UpstreamRepos --> Pins : concrete commit
Pins -> Pins : write the 40-hex sha into the pin variable, never a branch name
Operator -> Ansible : deploy with the updated pins
Ansible -> ControlNode : git checkout [pinned sha] detached and assert rev-parse HEAD equals the pin
ControlNode --> Ansible : checkout verified
Ansible -> Terra : rsync dependency payload and write .deploy-state with ref, commit and tree digest
Terra --> Ansible : dependency layer deployed at the pinned identity
Ansible --> Operator : report pinned refs and deployed shas
note over Pins
  refs-list and refs-update are planned in the dependency-layer plan and
  absent at base HEAD. A branch name is a moving target, so refs-update
  always records a concrete sha; the target never sees git or a key.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S6 - @Manilov VM lifecycle
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S6 — @Manilov VM lifecycle via Virt_scripts_bootstrap

actor Operator
participant "Container\nHomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol" as Container
participant "ScriptsDir\n~/.bookmarks/Virt_scripts_bootstrap" as ScriptsDir
participant "Libvirt\nqemu:///system" as Libvirt
participant "@Manilov\nHAOS 16.3 VM" as Manilov

Operator -> Container : docker exec -it --user ds13 HomeServer__HomeAssistant.NikolaiGogol bash
Operator -> ScriptsDir : cd /home/ds13/.bookmarks/Virt_scripts_bootstrap
Operator -> ScriptsDir : make install
ScriptsDir -> Libvirt : virt-install --connect qemu:///system ... --print-xml
Libvirt --> ScriptsDir : generated vmDefinition.xml
Operator -> ScriptsDir : make define-vm
ScriptsDir -> Libvirt : virsh -c qemu:///system define vmDefinition.xml
Operator -> ScriptsDir : make attach-devices
ScriptsDir -> Libvirt : virsh attach-device hass_qemu16 ZigbeeDongle.xml --config
Operator -> ScriptsDir : make start
note right of ScriptsDir
  start depends on define-vm and attach-devices,
  so either failure stops the start.
end note
ScriptsDir -> Libvirt : virsh start hass_qemu16
Libvirt -> Manilov : boot HAOS from the bind-mounted haos_ova.qcow2
Manilov --> Libvirt : domain running
Operator -> ScriptsDir : make info
ScriptsDir -> Libvirt : virsh dumpxml hass_qemu16
Libvirt --> ScriptsDir : domain XML
opt cleanup as-is
    Operator -> ScriptsDir : make undefine-vm
    ScriptsDir -> Libvirt : destroy and undefine hass_qemu16 --nvram --remove-all-storage
    Libvirt -> Manilov : remove the domain and its storage (destructive as-is)
end
note over ScriptsDir, Manilov
  The qcow2 survives container recreate because it is a host bind, but
  undefine-vm --remove-all-storage deletes it in the current as-is path.
  /var/lib/libvirt is not mounted, so domain definitions, NVRAM and
  virsh edit changes are lost on recreate. Redefine from vmDefinition.xml.
  install writes --network none, which disagrees with the tap0/MAC intent.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S7 - Post-deploy remote check, Phase 0 acceptance
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S7 — Post-deploy remote check (Phase 0 acceptance)

actor Operator
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir
participant "Docker daemon" as Docker

Operator -> Terra : ssh terra
Operator -> ScriptsDir : ls -A /zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts
ScriptsDir --> Operator : upstream files, no .git, .env mode 0600, .deploy-state
Operator -> ScriptsDir : bash -n each *.sh
ScriptsDir --> Operator : syntax OK
Operator -> Terra : cd _scripts and docker compose -f docker-compose-system.yml config -q
Terra -> Docker : validate compose with the rendered .env
Docker --> Terra : exit 0
Operator -> ScriptsDir : make -n image-name
ScriptsDir --> Operator : ds-omega/nikolaigogol with tag latest
note over Operator, ScriptsDir
  Three expected Phase 0 caveats, not S7 failures:
  - switch-nixos.sh hard-codes ~/.bookmarks/shared-configs/Unix_dotfiles,
    not the @terra checkout path.
  - the scripts call sudo docker; terra is uid 0 and sudo may be absent.
  - connect.sh has no REQUIRES_FUNCS; info and fatal may be undefined.
  S7 never runs switch-nixos.sh; it proves the bytes and validation only.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S8 - Dirty-target conflict
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S8 — Dirty-target conflict during scripts redeploy

actor Operator
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir
participant "Control node" as ControlNode
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra

Operator -> ScriptsDir : ad-hoc edit a script, compose file or .env
ScriptsDir --> Operator : local content changes, manifest untouched
Operator -> ControlNode : run TAGS=scripts redeploy
ControlNode -> Ansible : ansible-playbook -i hosts.ini deploy-nikolaigogol.yml --tags scripts
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash target tree excluding .env and .deploy-state*
ScriptsDir --> Ansible : current tree_sha256
Ansible -> Ansible : compare with .deploy-state tree_sha256
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : sha256sum -c .deploy-state.drift
Ansible --> Operator : fail with the drifted paths and the force hint
alt force=true
    Operator -> Ansible : re-run with -e nikolaigogol_scripts_force=true
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync overwrite with delete=false, render .env, hash deployed tree
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : write the new .deploy-state manifest
    ScriptsDir --> Ansible : new tree_sha256 recorded; extra files retained
    Ansible --> Operator : report forced deploy
else revert
    Operator -> ScriptsDir : revert the local edit
    Operator -> Ansible : re-run TAGS=scripts
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash matches .deploy-state
    ScriptsDir --> Ansible : clean target
    Ansible -> ScriptsDir : rsync, render .env and verify
    Ansible --> Operator : report clean deploy
end
note over ScriptsDir
  The manifest is updated only after a successful sync and hash.
  A failed drift guard leaves the previous payload and manifest intact.
  force=true is a one-run override and is not persisted in the manifest.
end note
@enduml


' ============================================================================
' S9 - Reverse flow: pull the on-@terra edits back
' ============================================================================
@startuml
autonumber
title S9 — Reverse flow: propagating on-@terra edits back

actor Operator
participant "Ansible" as Ansible
participant "Terra (TOS 6)" as Terra
participant "ScriptsDir\n/zterra/local-/Projects/@NikolaiGogol/_scripts" as ScriptsDir
participant "Control staging + worktree\n(pinned commit, disposable)" as Staging
participant "Upstream repo\nConvPlatProv__NikolaiGogol" as UpstreamRepos
participant "Pins\nsuperproject gitlink + refs-update" as Pins

Operator -> Ansible : re-run S1 (make -f Makefile.NixosScripts dry)
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : hash target tree and compare with .deploy-state
alt tree_sha256 matches
    Ansible --> Operator : clean; nothing to pull
else drift and force=false
    Ansible --> Operator : fail before rsync and list the FAILED paths (S8)
end
Operator -> Staging : create $PULL_ROOT/(stamp)/snapshot and /worktree
Operator -> Terra : rsync -az --checksum --no-owner --no-group (no --delete)
Terra -> ScriptsDir : read _scripts over SSH
ScriptsDir --> Staging : snapshot/ minus .env, .deploy-state*, .git, node_modules, .yarn/cache, result-*
Operator -> UpstreamRepos : PIN_SUB = git rev-parse (PIN_SUPER):@NikolaiGogol
Operator -> UpstreamRepos : git worktree add --detach (worktree) (PIN_SUB)
Operator -> Staging : rsync -a --checksum --delete --exclude=.git snapshot/ worktree/
Staging -> Staging : git add -A; diff --cached --stat, --summary, --numstat, --cached
Staging --> Operator : delta vs pin: added, modified, deleted, Bin, mode
alt review or bash -n rejects
    Operator -> Staging : fix in the disposable worktree and re-check
    Staging --> Operator : no commit, no push
else accepted
    Operator -> UpstreamRepos : git switch -c edge/terra-(date); one commit per logical fix
    UpstreamRepos -> UpstreamRepos : git push -u origin edge/terra-(date)
    UpstreamRepos --> Operator : branch pushed; PR opened, no auto-merge
end
Operator -> Pins : bump the @NikolaiGogol gitlink, commit, refs-update to the new pin
Pins --> Operator : new superproject sha recorded (scripts role has no pin var at base HEAD)
Operator -> Ansible : run S0 (TAGS=image,container,scripts) or S1 for scripts-only
Ansible -> ScriptsDir : re-sync, re-render .env, rewrite .deploy-state
ScriptsDir --> Operator : next run is clean; target still has no git and no key
note over Operator, Pins
  The target has no git and no credential; every step runs on the control node.
  Never force=true before the snapshot exists: forcing overwrites the only copy.
  The worktree is disposable; --delete is only ever used inside it.
  @NikolaiGogol is a submodule: a superproject-only commit records just a gitlink.
end note
@enduml
